- What are the performance trade-offs when migrating ML workloads to confidential GPUs?
- How do you handle key rotation in a multi-tenant TEE environment without service disruption?
- Design the incident response workflow when a tenant reports potential data exposure.
- How would you implement zero-trust networking between tenants in a shared inference cluster?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates practical NoSQL injection awareness in a common Node.js + MongoDB setup, focusing on concrete defenses and verification within a tight window.

## Key Concepts

- NoSQL injection
- Input whitelisting
- Safe query construction
- MongoDB schema validation
- Query sanitization tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Safe query builder example (Express handler)
const allowedFields = ['title','author','year'];
function buildQuery(params){
  const q = {};
  for (const [k,v] of Object.entries(params)) {
    if (allowedFields.includes(k) && typeof v === 'string') q[k] = v;
  }
  if (Object.keys(params).some(k => k.startsWith('$') || k.includes('.'))) {
    throw new Error('Invalid query');
  }
  return q;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test NoSQL injection resilience in CI?
- How can you extend this to handle nested documents or arrays?
- What DB-level controls (RBAC, JSON schema validation) would you add for defense in depth?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-time trading platforms demand ultra-low latency combined with robust replay protection across distributed microservices. Token binding mechanisms reduce impersonation risks while maintaining performance requirements critical to trading operations.

## Key Concepts
- Token binding and mutual TLS (mTLS) for connection-specific authentication
- Short time-to-live (TTL) tokens with audience-scoping for service isolation
- WebSocket connection nonces and replay prevention mechanisms
- Global revocation propagation strategies
- Comprehensive observability and audit trail implementation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate token and bind to nonce
function authorize(token, nonce, ctx){
  if (!isValidToken(token)) return false;
  if (!bindsToTLS(token, ctx)) return false;
  const session = createSecureSession(token, nonce);
  return session.isValid() && !isReplayAttempt(nonce);
}
```

